# Atoms in this file are deliberately masked: the ebuild is shipped
# in the overlay (so you can pin to it if you know you want it) but
# does not get installed by default. Unmask any of them in your own
# /etc/portage/package.unmask/rato-verlay if you want to opt in.
#
# Not masked (no package.unmask needed; all stay keyworded ~amd64):
#   net-fs/amazon-efs-utils-bin - the prebuilt AL2023 RPM repackage is the
#     default efs-utils of this overlay. The source sibling
#     net-fs/amazon-efs-utils (9999 live) no longer exists here: it failed
#     to build on GCC >= 14 (AWS-LC FIPS assembler error).
#   dev-util/claude-code-bin, dev-util/claude-desktop-bin - proprietary
#     (LICENSE=Anthropic-Claude-Terms): installing them still needs that
#     license in ACCEPT_LICENSE. Anthropic's Linux desktop app is a beta
#     packaged for Debian/Ubuntu.
#   dev-util/kirocrew-bin, dev-util/kiro-bin, dev-util/kiro-cli-bin.

# Ramin Torabi <16882282+RaminTorabi@users.noreply.github.com> (2026-05-24)
# VictoriaMetrics cluster mode (vminsert + vmselect + vmstorage) is shipped
# in the overlay for completeness and to give a clean upgrade path if a
# fleet ever outgrows the single-node sibling. It is NOT the recommended
# default: for ingestion rates below ~1M samples/sec the single-node
# variant (app-metrics/victoria-metrics{,-bin}) is simpler to operate and
# uses ~3x less memory. Unmask explicitly via /etc/portage/package.unmask
# if cluster mode is what you actually want; otherwise the single-node
# pair stays the daily driver.
#
# Same masking rationale applies to both the source-build and prebuilt
# variants - they are siblings, not alternatives, and the !! blocker
# between them prevents Portage from picking both at once.
app-metrics/victoria-metrics-cluster
app-metrics/victoria-metrics-cluster-bin

